{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Implementation detail for this story (the description carries the decisions). Cites on origin/main 083620b0.\n\nHooks, each a named module-level function in `_mcp_derive.py`:\n- PRE: `readonly_gate(label)` raises the exact current message `\"<label> is disabled: this server is read-only (REBAR_MCP_READONLY)\"`; `jira_sync_gate(label)`; `fsck_recover_gate`.\n- PINS: `include_inbound=True` (show_ticket), `return_alias=True` (create_ticket, create_idea, create_identity), `_creation_channel=\"mcp\"` (create_ticket, create_idea, create_identity, log_session), `report_only=ctx.readonly` (fsck; evaluated per call).\n- POST: `with_push` (`_with_push`), `ack` (`_ack`, drops None keys), `escalation_ack` (link_tickets), `description_warning_ack` (edit_ticket), `cross_session(id_param)` (`_cross_session`, key set only when non-None), `plan_review_health` (`rebar.audit.read.plan_review_health`, show_ticket), `discovery_rows(full)` (`_discovery_rows`, `_mcp_reads.py:264-285`; list_tickets and ready_tickets), `bound_list(tool)` (`_mcp_budget._bound_list_payload`; list_tickets, ready_tickets, search), `id_alias_only` (log_session).\n\nThe eight input overrides the table must carry (library annotation after the annotation story vs the MCP contract to preserve):\n| tool.param | library | MCP (pinned) |\n|---|---|---|\n| `list_tickets.full` | default `True` | default `False` (lean-by-default, story 98b8-5f08-1569-45cc, payload budget) |\n| `list_tickets.priority` | `int | str | None` (`_reads.py:148`; str is a CLI cast) | `int | None` |\n| `bridge_run.profile` | `str | None = None`, falls back to env `MODE` (`_bridge_runner.py:77`) | `str = \"dry-run\"` (safety default) |\n| `set_file_impact.impact` | `list[FileImpactEntry] | str` | `list[FileImpactEntry]` |\n| `set_verify_commands.commands` | `list[VerifyCommandEntry] | str` | `list[VerifyCommandEntry]` |\n| `sign_manifest.manifest` | `list[str] | str` | `list[str]` |\n| `attach_commits.commits` | `list[str | dict[str, Any]]` | `list[str]` |\n| `summary.ticket_ids` | `*ticket_ids: str` | `ticket_ids: list[str]`, calling `rebar.summary(*ticket_ids)` |\n| `transition_ticket` order | `force, reason, close_class` | `close_class, reason, force` (positional callers in `tests/unit/test_cross_session_mcp.py:278`) |\nEvery other parameter matches by name, type and default (KEYWORD_ONLY vs POSITIONAL has no schema effect). 0 of 48 MCP descriptions equal the library docstring (238 description lines, 14,865 chars), so every description is a verbatim `ToolSpec.description` string, not the docstring.\n\nThe ten declared divergences (carried verbatim from `tests/unit/mcp_library_parity_manifest.json` into each spec's `divergence` field): `comment_ticket` <- `comment` strips `allow_secret_pattern` (audited force override for the write-time secret screen, bug e7a9; MCP callers must not suppress the guard) and `source` (import provenance); `create_idea` <- `idea` pins `return_alias=True`, `_creation_channel=\"mcp\"`; `create_identity` <- `create_identity` pins the same two and does not expose `tags` (applied afterwards with `tag_ticket`); `create_ticket` <- `create_ticket` pins the same two and strips `source`; `edit_ticket` <- `edit_ticket` enumerates the eleven editable fields because `**fields` cannot be a JSON schema (a new editable library field must be added to the spec); `fsck` <- `fsck` derives `report_only` from the server's read-only gate rather than the caller; `log_session` <- `append_session_log` pins `_creation_channel=\"mcp\"`; `ready_tickets` <- `ready` adds the MCP-only `full` through `_discovery_rows` (story 98b8); `search` <- `search` fixes `full=False` (bug 494b-2dd3-e9d3-4fb0 payload budget); `show_ticket` <- `show_ticket` pins `include_inbound=True`.\n\nGolden capture command (run from the schema story's landed tree before writing derivation code; record the SHA in the test docstring):\n```\nREBAR_MCP_ALLOW_LLM=1 python -c 'import asyncio, json; from rebar.mcp_server import build_server; t = asyncio.run(build_server().list_tools()); print(json.dumps({x.name: {\"inputSchema\": x.inputSchema, \"description\": x.description, \"annotations\": x.annotations.model_dump() if x.annotations else None} for x in t}, indent=1, sort_keys=True))' > tests/interfaces/facades/mcp_tool_surface_golden.json\n```\n\nBaseline maintenance: this story deletes `scripts/check_mcp_library_parity.py`, a censused `ci_gate` mechanism, and its `make lint` invocation. Because `tests/unit/test_mechanism_delta.py:357-364` asserts the committed baseline equals the live tree, run `python scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py --update-stale` in the same change and commit `.github/mechanism-baseline.json` (operator-sanctioned on the epic; precedent commit 81da792). State the sanction in the commit message."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788806932992968545,"uuid":"7976650e-7370-43a5-a9ff-34d8969f11fb"}